  "faqQ1": "How does Root Flow work?",
  "faqA1": "You choose a category (like Health, Work, or Leisure) and a practice within it, start the timer, and log how much you practiced. Everything then shows up in the Dashboard and History so you can track your progress.",
  "faqQ2": "What is Match?",
  "faqA2": "It's the card-based screen (🌼) that suggests practices matching your current moment. Swipe sideways to see other suggestions, or tap one to get started.",
  "faqQ3": "What are UPs?",
  "faqA3": "UPs (Practice Units) measure how much you practiced an activity relative to its defined ideal time.",
  "faqQ4": "How do the Timer modes work?",
  "faqA4": "When starting a practice you can choose from 4 modes: Stopwatch (counts freely), Pomodoro (focus cycles with breaks), Manual (you type in time already practiced), and HIIT (high-intensity interval training).",
  "faqQ5": "What is the Balance Index?",
  "faqA5": "It's the Dashboard metric showing how evenly your time is spread across the categories you've practiced. The closer to 100%, the more balanced your routine.",
  "faqQ6": "What's the consciousness feedback after an activity?",
  "faqA6": "After finishing a practice, you rate how you felt (from automatic to flowing) and the difficulty level. This feeds the Dashboard's \"Flow vs Challenge\" chart, helping you spot which difficulty level gets you into flow most often.",
  "faqQ7": "Where is my data stored?",
  "faqA7": "Everything is stored locally on your device. Root Flow doesn't send anything to servers or the cloud.",
  "faqQ8": "How do I back up my data?",
  "faqA8": "Use \"Export data\" in the Settings menu to generate a backup file you can keep or share.",
  "faqQ9": "Can I use the app on another phone?",
  "faqA9": "Yes. Export your data on the current device and import the same file on the new phone.",
  "faqQ10": "Can I delete a default category or practice?",
  "faqA10": "Yes. In the Customize screen you can delete any category, even the default ones — deletion is permanent.",
  "faqQ11": "I lost my data, can I recover it?",
  "faqA11": "Only if you exported a backup before. Without a backup file, removed data can't be recovered.",

